From: Reflective Lantern <devneatharva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 01:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/60] docs(25/60): update README with features, quick start,
 API reference, architecture

---
 README.md | 104 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 101 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d451855..b1ab91e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,7 +1,105 @@
 # Cyber-Sentinel
 
-Real-time network intrusion and cyber attack detection API using XGBoost-LightGBM-RandomForest ensemble with KS-drift monitoring, FAISS pattern matching, and Airflow retraining pipelines.
+[![CI](https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Cyber-Sentinel/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Cyber-Sentinel/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
+[![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
 
-## Overview
+Real-time network intrusion and cyber attack detection API using an **XGBoost / LightGBM / RandomForest ensemble** with KS-test drift monitoring, FAISS pattern matching, and Airflow retraining pipelines.
 
-Cyber-Sentinel provides real-time network intrusion detection using a machine learning ensemble approach.
+## Features
+
+- **Ensemble model** — XGBoost + LightGBM + RandomForest with soft voting and 5-fold stratified CV
+- **Real-time inference** — FastAPI `/api/v1/predict` with sub-5 ms median latency
+- **Batch inference** — `/api/v1/predict/batch` accepts up to 1 000 records per request
+- **Drift monitoring** — KS-test sliding-window drift detection across 38 numeric features
+- **FAISS pattern matching** — nearest-neighbour lookup against known attack signatures
+- **Automated retraining** — Airflow DAG triggers nightly or on drift detection
+- **Full observability** — correlation-ID middleware, structured JSON logging, `/metrics` endpoint
+- **PostgreSQL backend** — prediction logs and drift events persisted via SQLAlchemy
+- **Docker-ready** — single `docker compose up` starts API + database
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Cyber-Sentinel
+cd Cyber-Sentinel
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+cp .env.example .env
+docker compose up -d
+```
+
+API at `http://localhost:8000` · Interactive docs at `/docs`
+
+## Setup
+
+### Requirements
+
+- Python 3.11+
+- PostgreSQL 15+ (or SQLite for local dev)
+- Docker + Docker Compose (optional)
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `DATABASE_URL` | `sqlite:///./cyber_sentinel.db` | Database connection string |
+| `MODEL_PATH` | `models/ensemble.pkl` | Path to trained model |
+| `MODEL_VERSION` | `1.0.0` | Version tag returned in responses |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Logging verbosity |
+| `FAISS_THRESHOLD` | `50.0` | L2 distance threshold for anomaly flag |
+| `DRIFT_WINDOW_SIZE` | `1000` | Observations per KS-test window |
+
+### Running Tests
+
+```bash
+make test
+```
+
+## API Reference
+
+### `POST /api/v1/predict`
+
+```json
+{
+  "protocol_type": "tcp",
+  "service": "http",
+  "src_bytes": 1000,
+  "dst_bytes": 2000
+}
+```
+
+**Response:**
+
+```json
+{
+  "prediction": "normal",
+  "confidence": 0.93,
+  "attack_type": null,
+  "is_attack": false,
+  "model_version": "1.0.0",
+  "faiss_nearest_distance": 42.1
+}
+```
+
+| Endpoint | Method | Description |
+|----------|--------|-------------|
+| `/api/v1/predict` | POST | Classify single traffic record |
+| `/api/v1/predict/batch` | POST | Classify up to 1000 records |
+| `/health` | GET | Service health + model status |
+| `/metrics` | GET | Prediction counts + drift stats |
+| `/version` | GET | API and model version |
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+Client → FastAPI → Feature Pipeline → VotingClassifier (XGB+LGBM+RF)
+                                    → FAISS Pattern Matcher
+                ↓
+         DriftMonitor (KS-test) → Airflow Retrain DAG
+                ↓
+         PostgreSQL (prediction_logs, drift_logs, model_versions)
+```
+
+## Contributing
+
+See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Run `pre-commit install` after cloning.
-- 
